RF.put("questb:b77",{"8637":{"id":8637,"t":"Deathdealer's Boots","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of Strife, 5 Crystal Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj. This quest also requires Neutral faction with the Brood of Nozdormu.\nQiraji Bindings of Command Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Strife Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"Qiraji magic is strong and ancient. The most powerful qiraji wield items of such might, they'd give pause even to a dragon.\nBring me the qiraji bindings of command and other minor components by and I'll create a set of powerful boots for you.\nYou will find them useful in the fight against the enemy.","rew":"You will receive:\nDeathdealer's Boots\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You've acquired the items I requested, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹name›. You've proven you're no ordinary mortal.\nI give you these with the confidence they'll aid you in crushing the vile qiraji.\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Rogue Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8637\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Deathdealer's Boots this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of Strife, 5 Crystal Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8557":{"id":8557,"t":"Drape of Unyielding Strength","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Martial Drape, 2 Onyx Idols, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Keyl Swiftclaw in Silithus. You must also obtain Revered reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Martial Drape General Rajaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Kurinnaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Onyx Idol Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Sandstalker 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 21000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"I'm glad to hear you're aiding us in our attack on Ahn'Qiraj, ‹name›. I can make you a protective item that'll be of assistance in the fight against our enemy, ‹class›.\nI shall need a Qiraji drape, which I'll resize for you of course. I'll also need idols and scarabs which I'll use to create a suitable clasp.\nI promise you won't be disappointed.","rew":"You will receive:\nDrape of Unyielding Strength\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring the materials for the cloak, ‹name›?","done":"Ah yes... this drape is immaculate.\nTake this cloak, ‹name›. May it protect you from the foul magic of the Qiraji.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.8,"y":39.5,"n":"Keyl Swiftclaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8797":{"id":8797,"t":"The Alliance Needs Your Help!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 650 experience instead of 9,500, 0.07 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Field Marshal Snowfall in Ironforge's Military Ward.","desc":"Hello, I'm glad that you've decided to hear me out. The Alliance needs all of the help that it can get to prepare for the Ahn'Qiraj War, and that means that we need you! Even now as we speak, official collectors are gathering the necessary material needed for the upcoming war, but we won't be able to meet our goals without your assistance, ‹name›!\nYou should go speak with the guy in charge, Field Marshal Snowfall. What do you say, ‹class›? Will you help out with the vital preparations?","rew":"Experience: 650\nDarnassus Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":42,"y":41.5,"n":"Master Sergeant Moonshadow","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.5,"y":34.7,"n":"Field Marshal Snowfall","e":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8397":{"id":8397,"t":"Claiming Arathi Basin","lv":59,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Winning a war is about more than just outsmarting and outfighting your opponent. Victory often comes down to simply producing more than your enemy.\nWhat we have in Arathi Basin is a sizeable supply of resources for whichever side manages to claim it first.\nIf the Alliance comes out victorious, it'll mean more swords and pikes for our troops. If the Horde were to win, those swords and pikes would still get made, they'd just be pointed at us! Now is the time to help the Alliance in Arathi Basin, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 3,200\n+50 reputation with The League of Arathor","back":"Tell me, what are the news from the front?","done":"Good work, soldier! Keep it up and we'll have the Horde running all the way back to Orgrimmar.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"1037":{"id":1037,"t":"Velinde Starsong","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Thyn'tel Bladeweaver at the Warrior's Terrace in Darnassus.","desc":"Velinde Starsong was my predecessor here in Ashenvale Forest. At first it seemed she had the situation in Felwood under control, but little by little her efforts faltered. One day, she simply disappeared.\nI was sent here to continue her work. I'm afraid I know nothing of the priestess, however. Perhaps Thyn'tel Bladeweaver, one of the commanders of the Sentinels, knows further details of her disappearance that I was not a party to.\nSurely she will understand the import of such information.","rew":"Experience: 600\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Velinde Starsong? That the priestess disappeared some time ago is almost certainly common knowledge. As to further details about the events that surrounded her departure... it would take good reason for me to divulge such information.\nAshenvale Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":22.2,"y":53,"n":"Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":61.8,"y":39.2,"n":"Thyn'tel Bladeweaver","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"3517":{"id":3517,"t":"Stealing Knowledge","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Tablet of Beth'Amara, the Tablet of Jin'yael, the Tablet of Markri, and the Tablet of Sael'hai before returning to Jediga in Azshara.\nTablet of Beth'Amara Tablet of Beth'Amara\nTablet of Jin'yael Tablet of Jin'yael\nTablet of Markri Tablet of Markri\nTablet of Sael'hai Tablet of Sael'hai","desc":"I admit, ‹name›, I've made the most of my situation in Azshara. Belgrom's punishment has had its share of benefits.\nBefore I left, I did some research and you would be surprised how many valuable items are lying around.\nI'll tell you more about my deals, and even give you a cut of the profits, if you help me gather some of them.\nThere are tablets throughout the Ruins of Eldarath to the east that I need. All four are named after Highborne wizards. Get them for me and we'll talk some more.","rew":"Experience: 5,100","back":"The tablets I'm having you gather should bring in a pretty copper or two to the right parties. I'll tell you who we need to deliver them to after you've found them. But I'm no fool... you'll get your share after I have proof that they've been delivered.\nSo get to it--we don't have all day. I might have to find someone else to help me.","done":"Perfect, ‹name›, and in good condition also. These should get us a good price from all the parties concerned.\nLet's not dawdle around here any longer than we have to. We have some money to make.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":22.6,"y":51.4,"n":"Jediga","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"717":{"id":717,"t":"Tremors of the Earth","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Sign of the Earth to activate the Pillars of Amethyst, Opal, and Diamond and obtain the Runestones.\nPlace the runestones in the Seal of the Earth to free Blacklash and Hematus.\nSlay them and return Blacklash's Bindings, the Chains of Hematus, and the Sign of the Earth to Garek.\nBlacklash's Bindings Blacklash\nChains of Hematus Hematus\nSign of the Earth Boss Tho'grun\nProvided: Sign of the Earth","desc":"It has become obvious that we cannot ensure that Blacklash and Hematus will remain imprisoned in Lethlor. That black dragons have taken up residence there, and that the ogres managed to steal the Sign indicates that more drastic measures will have to be taken.\nThe drakes' prison is maintained by three runestones that may only be retrieved using the Sign of the Earth. Those runestones can then be used to break the seal which imprisons them.\n‹name›... assure that their dreams are eternal.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBlazewind Breastplate Prismscale Hauberk Warforged Chestplate Mindburst Medallion\nExperience: 5,900\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Strong magics and powers held the drakes' prison for so long, but we cannot allow any possibility that Blacklash and Hematus may be released.","done":"No longer will the Kirin Tor need to worry over the prisoners of Lethlor. I will return to report success to my master. Krasus will no doubt be pleased.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":61.9,"y":54.3,"n":"Garek","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"97917":{"id":97917,"t":"Camping 101 enchanting","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Betty Quin in Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your enchanting skill to 20","desc":"Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Enchanted Lute. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nElwynn Forest Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":44.8,"y":63.2,"n":"Sam Sarsaparilla","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":43.2,"y":63.8,"n":"Betty Quin","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"8317":{"id":8317,"t":"Kitchen Assistance","lv":57,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Calandrath at Cenarion Hold needs a batch of 10 Smoked Desert Dumplings.\n10 Smoked Desert Dumplings","desc":"That recipe sure will come in handy. I'd better get to work so I can have some smoked desert dumplings ready for today. I could use a hand in making some, I'll make it worth your while.","rew":"Money: 1 70 1 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,000\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"How are those dumplings coming along?","done":"Excellent! You're a life saver. These dumplings turned out to be quite good. Didn't really expect such good taste from the Twilight's Hammer.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.9,"y":39.2,"n":"Calandrath","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["cooking"]},"94237":{"id":94237,"t":"Craftsmans writ crafted solid shot","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Crafted Solid Shot\n200 Crafted Solid Shot","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 200 Crafted Solid Shot, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Here to buy, or sell?","done":"I am glad you arrived when you did. A few Dragonmaw orcs stormed by the other day and gave me the stink eye.\nI ran out of ammunition on my way here. It's half the reason I haven't left this wretched place yet!\nThe other half being that I still have profits to make.\n<Kixxle greedily rubs his hands.>","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":50.1,"y":37.7,"n":"Kixxle","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94317":{"id":94317,"t":"Craftsmans writ dreamless sleep potion","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Dreamless Sleep Potion\nDreamless Sleep Potion","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Dreamless Sleep Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Dreamless Sleep Potion Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94317","cats":["crafting"]},"957":{"id":957,"t":"Bashal'Aran","lv":13,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Destroy the Ancient Moonstone Seal at the ancient flame in Ameth'Aran, then return to Asterion in Bashal'Aran.\nDestroy the seal at the ancient flame\nProvided: Ancient Moonstone Seal","desc":"It was the craft of one of the most powerful of the Highborne that created the seal that formed my prison. In Ameth'Aran, the ruins to the south that are twin to these, persists even today an ancient flame, blue in color. In this flame this seal could be destroyed.\nBe wary in the ruins, ‹name›...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nExplorer's Vest Vagabond Leggings Elven Wand\nExperience: 675\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"In truth, ‹name›, I am afraid... Afraid that your coming--all of this--is merely a figment of a deranged mind. Can you know the torture that this is? I... Please, you must go quickly.","done":"I am freed, ‹name›! I can now see with my own eyes the changes that have come to our world... Only bits and pieces have I known. To think that when I last walked freely, the Well still stood and the Highborne held court with Azshara, our beloved queen.\nI sense that my jailor, my former master, Athrikus, still lives... Already my feelings of hopelessness will give way into thoughts of vengeance.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":44.2,"y":36.3,"n":"Asterion","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"1437":{"id":1437,"t":"Vahlarriel's Search","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find and search Tyranis and Dalinda Malem's wagon in Desolace.","desc":"I am Vahlarriel, ‹name›. I've come here to discover the whereabouts of two missing nobles of a Darnassian merchant family--House Malem. The father of the house fears the worst, and I am to do everything I can to find his missing children. I have yet to start my search for Tyranis or Dalinda, but I am hopeful I shall not be here long.\nLast word tells of them passing through the Stonetalon Mountains a few weeks ago.\nIf you find their wagon, please, come find me immediately.","rew":"Experience: 1,950\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","done":"As you rummage around the remains of the wagon, it becomes obvious that it was attacked by both spells and weapons. The battle seemed one-sided and quick; there's no blood to be found, and no remains of any bodies.\nWhoever attacked the wagon was efficient and swift.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":66.4,"y":11.8,"n":"Vahlarriel Demonslayer","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":56.5,"y":17.8,"n":"Malem Chest","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"98397":{"id":98397,"t":"To darnassus","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Return to Darnassus and speak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave.","desc":"The time has come for us to part ways once again, young one, as the application of your lessons takes you back to whom that sent you to me. It would seem your instructor, Mathrengyl Bearwalker, has found a worthy pupil in you. I believe I see one as well. Heed his lessons and you shall soon be able to draw upon the Great Cat Spirit to take its shape.\nGo back to whence you came. When the time is right, we will meet again.","done":"Welcome back, Turq. I can sense you have met with the Great Cat Spirit and have successfully completed the trial. All druids must pass a trial given by this spirit, though the trials vary by generation. I am proud you have passed and have heeded the wisdom of the Great Cat Spirit. It is an ancient spirit that is as deadly as it is playful, though I can sense you understand the spirit's nature already.\nI will now instruct you on how to take the shape of the cat.\nMoonglade Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.4,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.2,"y":8,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"97277":{"id":97277,"t":"Grund and gozwin","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Grund and Gozwin's camp in the hills to the northwest. Recover Gozwin's Mechanic's Log and kill the Snow Leopard Prowler.\nGozwin's Mechanic's Log\nSnow Leopard Prowler slain","desc":"Oi, had me back turned gettin' the boar roast ready when I heard me pal Gozwin screamin' fer his life!\nWicked fangs and a blur are all I saw when I turned. Such huge paws! A snow leopard was draggin' its gnomish catch away. I grabbed me shotgun and fired above the beast. It dropped him and sprinted off.\nLuckily, it hadn't done more than give ol' Goz some deep scratches.\nHead back to camp in the northwestern hills and retrieve Gozwin's Mechanic's Log. Kill that snow leopard too if you see it!","rew":"You will receive:\nCanvas Latchbag\nExperience: 410\n+75 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles\n+75 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Poor Goz is more concerned for his mecha-walker than himself. Says if anyone gets a hold of that mechanic's log he's greased. Hah! That's why I told him he should just leave his work at home!","done":"Aye, I'm not surprised to hear that snow leopard was makin' a meal of the boar we were fixin' fer roastin'!\nGoz will have one less thing to stress about now that you brought back his log book. Maybe now he can focus all his energy on gettin' back on his feet.\nThanks, Missing. Take a little something as a token of my appreciation, fer makin' the trek, and fer protectin' the hills.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.6,"y":67.4,"n":"Grund Drokda","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"317":{"id":317,"t":"Stocking Jetsteam","lv":6,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 4 Chunks of Boar Meat and 2 Thick Bear Furs, and deliver them to Pilot Bellowfiz at Steelgrill's Depot.\n4 Chunk of Boar Meat Dire Mottled Boar 97.7 % , Elder Mottled Boar 82.4 % , Mangy Mountain Boar 81.9 % , Corrupted Mottled Boar 81.6 % and 4 more\n2 Thick Bear Fur Young Black Bear 80 % , Ice Claw Bear 80 %","desc":"I'm preparing to start a mission for the Siege Brigade. It's a long one, and I need to stock Jetsteam with a month's worth of supplies. So while Steelgrill is working on my tank, can you do some hunting for me?\nI'll need some fur for bedding, and boar meat for food. You can get meat from boars and fur from the bears... you can find them both in the snow fields south of the Grizzled Den.","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 675\n+150 reputation with Ironforge\n+150 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Preparations are going well. How goes your hunting?","done":"By Magni's beard, you sure did a lot of hunting!! Thank you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":49.4,"y":48.4,"n":"Pilot Bellowfiz","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"96877":{"id":96877,"t":"Halikors hoof","lv":12,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver Halikor's Hoof to Orgrimmar.\nProvided: Halikor's Hoof","desc":"The enormous hoof serves as proof of your victory over the mighty lizard.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 675\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Yes?","done":"What a trophy, ‹class›! That must have been some fight!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":63,"y":45,"n":"Kamari","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"157":{"id":157,"t":"Deliver the Thread","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Ghost Hair Thread to Abercrombie, in his shack north of the Raven Hill Cemetery.\nGhost Hair Thread\nProvided: Ghost Hair Thread","desc":"Here is your thread, ‹name›. It has a thousand uses, from binding evil spirits to sewing life into inanimate objects.","rew":"Money: 13 0 gold, 13 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,450","back":"I need to string the Ghost Hair Thread along my door and my windows to keep out unwanted spirits. Did you get it for me?","done":"Delightful! This will do splendidly...\nHere, good ‹name›, take this as payment for your honorable deed.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.8,"y":45.3,"n":"Madame Eva","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":28.1,"y":31.5,"n":"Abercrombie","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"5517":{"id":5517,"t":"Chromatic Mantle of the Dawn","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 25 Argent Dawn Valor Tokens to Quartermaster Breechlock at Light's Hope Chapel, Eastern Plaguelands.\n25 Argent Dawn Valor Token\nReach 42000 reputation with Argent Dawn","desc":"Brother/Sister ‹name› - your deeds on behalf of the Argent Dawn are far too numerous to be recounted easily. As a fitting tribute, I'll part with one of our special Chromatic Mantles of the Dawn - a version that protects the wearer from all forms of resistible magic simultaneously. Chromatic Mantles of the Dawn are reserved for only the mightiest of the Dawn's heroes!\nBring to me twenty-five valor tokens as a sign of tribute, and I'll give you the finest of all our mantles.","rew":"You will receive:\nChromatic Mantle of the Dawn\nExperience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Salutations, mighty priest! Have you brought the valor tokens I asked of you? Once you hand them to me, I will issue you your own Chromatic Mantle of the Dawn.","done":"Most impressive, ‹name› - the Chromatic Mantle of the Dawn is now yours!\nAs long as you maintain Exalted status with the Argent Dawn, you will be able to purchase additional Chromatic Mantles. They will be made available to you immediately from any of the Dawn's quartermasters.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.8,"y":50.2,"n":"Quartermaster Miranda Breechlock","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9197":{"id":9197,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Gnomish Battle Chicken","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 4 Gnomish Battle Chickens and the Craftsman's Writ - Gnomish Battle Chicken - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Gnomish Battle Chicken\n4 Gnomish Battle Chicken\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Gnomish Battle Chicken","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order EN-0:\n4 Gnomish Battle Chickens.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"Why are you smiling? What's so funny? Listen, mister/missy, a gnomish battle chicken is a very important unit and not to be taken lightly - EVER. We send these in to areas that might be heavily plagued or infested and they clean up any plagued insects or carrion maggots that might still be fluttering about. Everybody knows that robots are immune to the plague.\nI bet you don't feel so smart now, do you? Big dummy...","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"7677":{"id":7677,"t":"White Stallion Exchange","lv":1,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"If you bring me your white stallion, I'll trade you for one from the new herd. The new horse will be just as fast as your old one, but have a different look to it. You can look at the swift steeds here to see what it will look like.\nMUST PAY 500 Gold too....\nWhite Stallion Bridle","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSwift Brown Steed Swift Palomino Swift White Steed","back":"If you bring me your white stallion, I'll trade you for one from the new herd. The new horse will be just as fast as your old one, but have a different look to it. You can look at the swift steeds here to see what it will look like.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":84.2,"y":65.5,"n":"Katie Hunter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"557":{"id":557,"t":"Bracers of Binding","lv":34,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 Bracers of Earth Binding to Keeper Bel'varil in Tarren Mill.\n4 Bracers of Earth Binding Elemental Slave 80 %","desc":"The Magus will be busy studying those stone tokens you gathered, but I know he'll eventually want examples of their counterpart: bracers of binding. These are set around the wrists of actual elementals, and bind them into the mage's service.\nHunt elementals in the ruins of Dalaran and gather their Bracers of Earth Binding, and the Magus will be pleased.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,700\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Elementals are tough quarry, but I know you're up to the task. Do you have those bracers of binding?","done":"You found them. I trust the elementals from which you removed these bracers were amenable?\nHm...death has not only stopped my heart, but robbed me of my comedic timing, it seems.\nWell thank you, ‹name›. You serve the Magus, and hence the Dark Lady, well.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.5,"y":20.9,"n":"Keeper Bel'varil","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"3117":{"id":3117,"t":"Etched Sigil","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Etched Sigil and speak to Ayanna Everstride at the top of Aldrassil in Shadowglen.\nEtched Sigil\nProvided: Etched Sigil","desc":"This sigil was given to me by a messenger from our hunter trainer, Ayanna. It seems Ayanna would have words with you when you have a moment. Read it and bring it to her afterwards.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"You've arrived, and none too soon, ‹name›. Welcome to Shadowglen.\nI trust my sigil found you in good spirits and health?\nAs I said previously, I am here to train you as a ‹class›; to tame beasts to aid you in battle; to use a bow with unerring accuracy; to respect the lands which we call home and also the lands beyond.","done":"As you experience what Shadowglen has to teach you, come see me--I will be able to help you understand more about your role as a ‹class› and what you are capable of.\nThese are dangerous times, ‹name›, do not take for granted the skill of your pets--there are things in this world more dangerous than you can imagine. Go with Elune and return to me again.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":58.7,"y":44.3,"n":"Conservator Ilthalaine","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":58.7,"y":40.4,"n":"Ayanna Everstride","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"637":{"id":637,"t":"Sully Balloo's Letter","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Sully Balloo's Letter to Sara Balloo.\nSully Balloo's Letter\nProvided: Sully Balloo's Letter","desc":"The waterlogged and war-torn envelope dissolves in your hands, leaving you with a few pages of a letter in your grasp, written with painstaking care.\nThe letter is addressed to a Mrs. Sara Balloo of Ironforge and begins, \"My dear Sara....\"","rew":"Experience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"You look as though you have traveled a great distance and seen much turmoil in your time, ‹class›. These times we live in are trying on the soul. What news do you bring to me now?","done":"You say you saw my Sully pinned beneath the icy waters? Say it isn't so!\nLet me read what he wrote....\nArathi Highlands Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":44.3,"y":92.9,"n":"Waterlogged Envelope","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.3,"y":31.9,"n":"Sara Balloo","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"237":{"id":237,"t":"In Defense of the King's Lands","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Mountaineer Gravelgaw in the southern guard tower wants you to kill 10 Stonesplinter Skullthumpers and 10 Stonesplinter Seers and report back to him.\nStonesplinter Skullthumper slain : 0/ 10\nStonesplinter Seer slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Mountaineer Cobbleflint had nothing but good things to say about you, ‹race›. For that reason I am going to entrust upon you a mission of utmost importance. We need to keep pressure on the invading Trogg forces until our Dwarven brethren return from the Alliance front.\nSet forth into the southern hills and kill 10 Stonesplinter Skullthumpers and 10 Stonesplinter Seers. Your attacks will buy us some time. Report back when your mission is complete.","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Lesser Healing Potion\nMoney: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"We need more time, ‹race›. Your orders are to kill 10 Stonesplinter Skullthumpers and 10 Stonesplinter Seers. Keep the enemy under pressure until we are granted reinforcements. This is no time for idle behavior.","done":"You accomplished your mission well, ‹race›. The King himself would be proud.\nThe reinforcements promised to us never showed, however. Apparently the Alliance front is a sea of crimson from the blood of our fallen brethren. The news of the losses leaves a bitter taste in one's mouth. But we must not let their deaths go for naught. We must rally in these grim times and bring glory back to the Alliance.\nSpeak with Mountaineer Wallbang for reassignment. You're needed now more than ever.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":23.5,"y":76.4,"n":"Mountaineer Gravelgaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8877":{"id":8877,"t":"Firework Launcher","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Coin of Ancestry","rew":"You will receive:\nSchematic: Firework Launcher Lunar Festival Fireworks Pack","back":"Although rockets are a wonderful way to celebrate, in order to see their glory... they must be fired from a launcher.\nBring me coins of ancestry and I can offer you the knowledge to create rocket launchers like the ones you see in Moonglade.","done":"Here you are, ‹name›. Here is the schematic to create a firework launcher. Place launchers where you wish to celebrate, and then welcome your friends to join you!","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":53.8,"y":35.3,"n":"Fariel Starsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8717":{"id":8717,"t":"Moonwarden the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, ‹name›. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.4,"y":30.7,"n":"Elder Moonwarden","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"99197":{"id":99197,"t":"A donation of silk","lv":60,"min":26,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"60 Silk Cloth","back":"The Windshapers presently find ourselves in need of silk cloth. If you could spare sixty pieces of silk then we should be able to reach our goal with the support of others.\nA fine gift such as silk would certainly increase your honor and esteem amongst the Windshapers!\nIf you have the sixty pieces of silk cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":34.2,"y":22.4,"n":"Oura Stormspinner","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9117":{"id":9117,"t":"Belt of Faith","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Father Inigo Montoy at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Belt of Faith if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Belt, 8 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 2 Arcane Crystals and 2 Mooncloth.\nDesecrated Belt Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Heigan the Unclean 0 % in Naxxramas , Noth the Plaguebringer 0 % in Naxxramas\n8 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n2 Arcane Crystal Hakkari Thorium Vein 5.8 % , Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Ooze Covered Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Small Thorium Vein 2.6 % and 4 more\n2 Mooncloth","desc":"<Father Montoy makes some strange gestures in the air in front of you.>\nBlessed boy/girl, have you found the vestments of the fallen? The poor souls whose last breaths were taken on the field of battle - stripped of everything including their dignity.\nBring me the desecrated remnants of the departed along with reagents of purification and you shall know faith.","rew":"You will receive:\nBelt of Faith\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Belt of Faith.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Father Inigo Montoy","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9037":{"id":9037,"t":"Dreadnaught Helmet","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Korfax at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Dreadnaught Helmet if you bring him the following items: 1 Desecrated Helmet, 15 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 5 Arcanite Bars and 1 Nexus Crystal.\nDesecrated Helmet\n15 Wartorn Plate Scrap Infectious Ghoul 22.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 21.6 % in Naxxramas , Plagued Deathhound 21.3 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 20.8 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n5 Arcanite Bar\nNexus Crystal","desc":"During your battles with the Scourge in Naxxramas, should you come across desecrated battlements and wartorn plate scraps, return them to me and I shall craft for you a piece of armor worn by heroes.","rew":"You will receive:\nDreadnaught Helmet\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Dreadnaught Helmet.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":72,"y":48.5,"n":"Korfax, Champion of the Light","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"7837":{"id":7837,"t":"Additional Runecloth","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","back":"Greetings once again, ‹name›! Our need for runecloth is constant, and we can always use additional resources if you are willing to part with them. For an additional stack of twenty runecloth, I will make sure that you are recognized for your continuing efforts on behalf of the Darkspear Trolls.\nWhenever you are ready to hand in the stack of runecloth, I'll accept it.","done":"‹name› - without heroes like you working on behalf of the trolls, we'd surely suffer. Thank you for your continued efforts!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":37.7,"y":87.9,"n":"Vehena","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"8957":{"id":8957,"t":"Anthion's Parting Words","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Boots of Elements, Kilt of Elements and Pauldrons of Elements.\nBoots of Elements Highlord Omokk 0 %\nKilt of Elements Baron Rivendare 0 % in Stratholme\nPauldrons of Elements Gyth 0 %\nProvided: Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together. Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.\nI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","rew":"You will receive:\nBoots of The Five Thunders Kilt of The Five Thunders Pauldrons of The Five Thunders\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're back, ‹name›. You must tell me all about what you've found out. But first let us arrange for your reward.","done":"I can't believe our lives are all but forfeit all because of a stupid medallion! And you're sure Anthion mentioned Bodley?\nWell, you've done your job so let's get your reward out of the way.\nEastern Plaguelands Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"5677":{"id":5677,"t":"Arcane Feedback","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.","desc":"As much as I'd like to show you our own special teachings of the Light, it is not our place. Your place is back in Stormwind with your own kind, ‹name›... for now. Believe me, I mean no offense. When you return to High Priestess Laurena in the Cathedral of Light you'll understand what I'm talking about--the time has come for your race to prepare you for the future; to separate yourself from others that follow a similar path.","rew":"You will learn: Desperate Prayer\nExperience: 390","done":"We were forced to learn some magics to protect us from what is commonly called our greatest enemy: the arcane.\nI would teach you a spell to help you defend yourself and your companions from those who would wield such power.\nDun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55,"y":22.4,"n":"High Priest Rohan","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":44.6,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"1517":{"id":1517,"t":"Call of Earth","lv":4,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 270 experience instead of 250, 1.08 times as much.","obj":"Find Spirit Rock and drink the Earth Sapta.\nProvided: Earth Sapta","desc":"A sapta is a drink created to bind our spirits to the elements. Fused with magic, the potion will allow the strong willed to see the elements as no one else can. Your spirit will be connected to the element the sapta was created for, and only a select few shaman know the recipe.\nThe sapta is always drunk in a holy place, and never anywhere else--remember that.\nSeek out Spirit Rock southwest of here--it is found at the end of the Hidden Path. Drink your sapta there, and... well, you shall see.","rew":"Experience: 270","done":"Ah... ‹name›... pleased is the earth to have you here.\nBound together in body and spirit, you will go forward knowing that the mountains are your strength; the plains, your patience; and the world itself your essence.\nStanding before the earth humbly is all that is required of you for you to pass this rite. But the others are not as passive. They may be chaotic and often violent, but such is the nature of the elements. Dual natures opposing one another, you must come to learn these things intricately.\nDurotar Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.4,"y":69.2,"n":"Canaga Earthcaller","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":44,"y":76.2,"n":"Minor Manifestation of Earth","e":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":52,"y":80.4,"n":"Minor Manifestation of Earth","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"93037":{"id":93037,"t":"Outing outcasts","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan, and bring 1 Necromantic Garb to Nerlokh at the entrance of the Valley of Bones.\nNecromantic Garb\nGelkis Clan Centaur:\nLevel 40 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 36 38 43 51 Side Both factions Quest ID 93037","cats":["shendralas"]},"477":{"id":477,"t":"Border Crossings","lv":14,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the contents of one of the Dalaran wizards' crates. You will find Pyrewood Village to the south.","desc":"As you may know, the town of Ambermill remains a source of human opposition, mainly through the support they receive from the wizards of Dalaran.\nI don't know what their plan is, but for them to show interest in a backwater village like Ambermill indicates that it must have some greater importance.\nThey've been shipping crates by the wagon from Hillsbrad. Many of those supplies end up at a small camp north of Pyrewood Village. Retrieve the contents of a crate and return them to me.","rew":"Experience: 975\n+100 reputation with Undercity","done":"<Prying open the lid of the crate, you find an assortment of carefully-packed objects. On the top of the crate lies a bundle of maps, yellowing with age, that appear to depict Silverpine Forest and other parts of western Lordaeron.\nUnderneath the maps is a mysterious-looking magical pendant.>","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44,"y":40.9,"n":"Shadow Priest Allister","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":49.9,"y":60.3,"n":"Dalaran Crate","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"84397":{"id":84397,"t":"Northern kalimdor a comprehensive guide","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Northern Kalimdor - A Comprehensive Guide","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nNorthern Kalimdor - A Comprehensive Guide (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.6,"y":79.4,"n":"Jennea Cannon","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.4,"y":32.4,"n":"Oran Snakewrithe","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"397":{"id":397,"t":"You Have Served Us Well","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Zggi, the servant of Zardeth the Blackclaw, to claim your reward.","desc":"I hear Lord Wishock enjoyed his beverage.\nYou have served us well, ‹name›. The Warlocks of Stormwind will be able to practice our ways without disturbance, thanks to you. For your efforts, I have prepared a special gift for you. Speak with my servant, Zggi, and claim your reward.","rew":"You will receive:\nDread Mage Hat\nExperience: 250","done":"Master says give gift to ‹name›. Zggi wants to keep nice gift but Zggi knows better than to betray Master.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":40.1,"y":85.3,"n":"Zardeth of the Black Claw","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":40.2,"y":85.3,"n":"Zggi","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"8077":{"id":8077,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Demoniac's Robes","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing a Primal Hakkari Kossack. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Revered with the Zandalar Tribe.\nAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Kossack\nReach 21000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"The ultimate symbol of power amongst the tribe is the garb we wear in battle. A demoniac's robes have fused fine runecloth and devastatingly powerful mojo into a single fabric. The visage of the robe is said to instill fear into the minds of all who see it... especially the demons that the demoniac will eventually dominate.\nFrom Zul'Gurub, you must bring me a very specific set of the Paragons of Power. It will be difficult... but your success will assure you of acquiring a robe for yourself.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Demoniac's Robe\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"The Paragons of Power... you have returned with them? Only once we have them will we share the ultimate symbol of demoniac power with you, ‹name›.","done":"Impressive - your victory in Zul'Gurub has assured us - nay, the world - that Hakkar will not prevail. The time may come when you face the Blood God directly... and should this come to pass know that your reverence is assured amongst the Zandalar tribe.\nOh, and this simple robe should help out too I think.\n<Al'tabim winks knowingly at you.>","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"877":{"id":877,"t":"The Stagnant Oasis","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Tonga at The Crossroads, after investigating the Stagnant Oasis.\nTest the Dried Seeds\nProvided: Dried Seeds","desc":"Like the one you found at the Forgotten Pools, there may be fissures at the other oases in the Barrens. If so, then perhaps the fissures are the oases' source of life.\nWe must test this.\nHere, take these seeds. They are dead and infertile, but take them to the Stagnant Oasis to the southeast. If there is a fissure there, then place the seeds within it...and observe.","rew":"Experience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Have you been to the Stagnant Oasis? Was there a fissure beneath its waters?","done":"Your findings are amazing! The seeds I gave you were dried, and dead. Whatever rests under these oases can create life from nothing!\nWe must study this more...","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.3,"y":31.9,"n":"Tonga Runetotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"77":{"id":77,"t":"A Sticky Situation","lv":48,"min":42,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Recover 10 bottles of Hinterlands Honey Ripple from the crates located around the abandoned Horde base in Skulk Rock.\n10 Hinterlands Honey Ripple Horde Supply Crate","desc":"I possess original packaging materials for the ripple Dran Droffers seeks. I will assist you in packaging the ripple for Malton's abrasive father... for a fee of two additional bottles of said ripple. They are located in crates found in the abandoned Horde base near Skulk Rock.\nIt will be an arduous task, to wit; foul slimes and oozes will be found sticking to the ruins; rumor has it they are led by some sort of master ooze. Regardless, procure the ripple and return to me here for packaging.","rew":"Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"I trust that your arrival here at our camp is to deliver the bottles of ripple that are integral to the task at hand, yes?","done":"Finely executed, ‹name›. I am glad you had enough foresight not to bruise the delicacy of the ripple. There is nothing worse than the bouquet of ripple that has been jostled about needlessly.\nIt will take a moment for the magic to be wrought over this precious cargo. Actually, no magic is involved; I merely have some empty packaging for Hinterlands Honey Ripple. Our chicanery shall turn these bottles into an alcoholic treasure of the ages.\nOnward - for great booze!","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":26.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Gilveradin Sunchaser","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"2877":{"id":2877,"t":"Skulk Rock Clean-up","lv":48,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Green Sludges and 10 Jade Oozes, and then report back to Fraggar Thundermantle in Aerie Peak.\nGreen Sludge slain : 0/ 10\nJade Ooze slain : 0/ 10","desc":"We Wildhammers remember the past, more than our brothers in Ironforge. If you want to make friends here, then you get your hands dirty for us!\nThe Horde abandoned their positions in the Hinterlands around Skulk Rock; it's now overrun with nasty sludges and oozes. We've got plans on that area, but first we need a clean-up crew to make a hole for us.\nThat's where you come in, Sunshine! Head down there and take out ten green sludges and ten jade oozes, then report back to me here. Move out!","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Wildhammer Clan","back":"Make no effort to negotiate the mission at hand, ‹race›! If the gods had wanted those oozes killed, they would have miracled it done by now, wouldn't they?!","done":"Well look at you, helping out the Wildhammers! You're a ‹class› of action, and action is what we respect around here.\nYour little clean-up mission is a lot more important than you might think it is. With folks thinning out the oozes and sludges, we'll be able to extend our sphere of influence in no time. Here - have a little something in addition to just making new friends here in Aerie Peak!","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":14.8,"y":44.6,"n":"Fraggar Thundermantle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"1117":{"id":1117,"t":"Rumors for Kravel","lv":36,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Goblin Rumors to Kravel Koalbeard in the Shimmering Flats.\nGoblin Rumors\nProvided: Goblin Rumors","desc":"I had to use some of my favors, and gave away a rare bottle of elven wine, and did some heavy deducing myself! But I found the information you seek.\nHere, I wrote a letter with some very interesting bits on our friend, Nazz Steamboil. Do with it what you will -- it's too dangerous for me to use.\nJust don't tell anyone where you got it!","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,500","back":"Did you get anything on Nazz Steamboil? Anything he might want to keep a secret??","done":"Well well! This is interesting... very interesting. Heh, perhaps I should bow to the goblin pilot the next time I see him.\nThis is worth plenty, ‹name›. I'm sure Nazz will pay a small fortune to keep his secret... a secret.\nStranglethorn Vale Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.9,"y":77.2,"n":"Krazek","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":77.8,"y":77.3,"n":"Kravel Koalbeard","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1197":{"id":1197,"t":"The Sacred Flame","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Cloven Hoof for Rau Cliffrunner at the Freewind Post.\nCloven Hoof Ancient Brazier\nProvided: Filled Etched Phial","desc":"Using the water you brought, you will be able to temporarily douse the flame that holds the centaur relic. It will not work permanently, however, so you will have to be quick about it.\nYou will find Splithoof Crag, the centaurs' stronghold, to the north of here. The flame is kept in Splithoof Hold, a heavily guarded part of the crag.\nBe careful, though, the Galak centaur have great numbers here, and will be rather reluctant to surrender something so dear to them.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCliffrunner's Aim Azure Sash\nExperience: 2,350\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"I am eager to put my hands upon the Cloven Hoof. Have you taken it yet?","done":"I sense a strange energy emanating from the Hoof... I have no doubt that we will discover surprising new information about the centaur from its study.\nMy thanks, ‹name›. Now I must begin to decipher the mysteries you have brought to me.\nThousand Needles The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":46.1,"y":51.7,"n":"Rau Cliffrunner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"65597":{"id":65597,"t":"The binding","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Using the Lovers' Hearts, summon and subdue an incubus, then return the Lovers' Hearts to Carendin Halgar in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.\nSummoned Incubus slain\nProvided: Lovers' Hearts","desc":"The time has come at last. Bring the hearts to the summoning circle below. Place them at its center and call forth the incubus.\nThe demon will not be pleased when it realizes that you have tempted it into a trap. Do not fall prey to its beguilement, ‹name›. You must subdue it fully.\nOnly then can I teach you the spell to bind it to your will.","rew":"You will receive:\nSmall Soul Pouch\nExperience: 1,550","back":"The incubus possesses martial prowess, but its illusory charms are its most potent weapon. Falter for even a moment, and the demon will seize upon the opportunity to enthrall you.\nDo not let it, ‹name›.","done":"Impressive. Very impressive. The sayaad specialize in preying upon mortals. Many a ‹class› has thought themselves strong enough to command one, only to find themselves being commanded instead.\nThis trial did not break you, ‹name›, and your efforts have earned your reward. I will teach you the spell to summon the incubus.\nUndercity Stormwind City Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":85,"y":25.6,"n":"Carendin Halgar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]}});